.TH QUEST\-STREAM 1 "2026-10-10" "quest-stream" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
quest-stream \- serve video folders to a Meta Quest over USB
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quest-stream
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B quest-stream
serves three local video directories to a Meta Quest headset over the USB cable,
using
.BR miniserve (1)
bound to
.IR 127.0.0.1 ,
and keeps an
.BR adb (1)
reverse tunnel alive so the headset can reach the host as
.IR localhost .
.P
The folders exported are
.IR /mnt/data_storage/ctbrec ,
.IR /mnt/data_storage/Handbraked ,
and
.IR /mnt/data_storage/compressing .
Each is staged as a symlink under
.I ~/.local/share/quest-stream
so a single
.B miniserve
instance can serve them. The script then re-applies
.B adb reverse
on a short interval, because reverse mappings are dropped whenever the headset
reconnects. The server binds to the loopback interface only, so it is never
reachable from the LAN.
.P
Point DeoVR (or the headset browser) at
.I http://127.0.0.1:8080
and all three folders appear as browsable listings. DeoVR's
.B Stream
field also accepts direct file URLs such as
.IR http://127.0.0.1:8080/Handbraked/clip.mp4 .
.P
The script runs either in the foreground or as the
.BR systemd (1)
user unit
.IR quest-stream.service ,
which starts it at login.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and the DeoVR URL, then exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QUEST_STREAM_PORT
TCP port bound on
.IR 127.0.0.1 .
Default:
.BR 8080 .
.TP
.B QUEST_STREAM_ROOT
Directory where the symlink staging tree is created. Default:
.IR ~/.local/share/quest-stream .
.SH BEHAVIOUR
.SS What it does
.IP \(bu 2
Creates or refreshes symlinks in the staging directory for each source folder.
.IP \(bu 2
Runs a background loop that re-applies the
.B adb reverse
tunnel every 15 seconds while a device is connected.
.IP \(bu 2
Executes
.B miniserve
in the foreground; stopping the script stops the server.
.SS Requirements
.IP \(bu 2
.BR miniserve (1)
(from the
.B miniserve
package).
.IP \(bu 2
.BR adb (1)
(from
.BR android-tools ).
.IP \(bu 2
A Meta Quest with Developer Mode enabled and USB debugging authorized.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run with defaults:
.IP
.EX
quest-stream
.EE
.P
Use a different port:
.IP
.EX
QUEST_STREAM_PORT=9000 quest-stream
.EE
.P
Control the user service:
.IP
.EX
systemctl \-\-user status quest-stream
systemctl \-\-user restart quest-stream
systemctl \-\-user stop quest-stream
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /mnt/data_storage/ctbrec
First exported folder.
.TP
.I /mnt/data_storage/Handbraked
Second exported folder (also shows the nested
.I Handbraked
bind mount).
.TP
.I /mnt/data_storage/compressing
Third exported folder.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/quest-stream
Symlink staging directory served by miniserve.
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/quest-stream.service
User unit that starts the server at login.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Server stopped normally.
.TP
.B 1
Missing dependency, or a source directory does not exist.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR miniserve (1),
.BR adb (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
